.TH 3DPOLY 1
.SH NAME
3dpoly \- filled polygons, a depth buffer and a mirror
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/3dpoly
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I 3DPoly
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/3DPoly.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Three parallel quadrilaterals at three depths, in green, red and blue,
and two more joining them, dithered so the connecting faces read as
blends of the faces they join.  The whole tumbles on three rates \- 2.1,
1.1 and 0.5 degrees a frame \- which share no common factor, so it never
repeats.
.PP
The other half is symmetry.  The device context is given two points, the
centre of the window and the cursor, and everything drawn afterwards is
drawn again reflected in the line through them, which the light blue line
marks.  Move the mouse and the mirror swings.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "mouse move"
Swing the mirror
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/3dpoly.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR wm (1)
